---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Electricity Cheat Sheet | Free Circuits, Ohm's Law, Power"
  description="Complete electricity cheat sheet with circuits, Ohm's law, and power formulas. Free download for physics and engineering students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Electricity<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Circuits, Ohm's law, and power. From basic circuits to AC analysis.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Basic Circuits</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Ohm's Law</h3>
        <pre><code>V = IR
I = V/R
R = V/I

V = voltage (volts)
I = current (amps)
R = resistance (ohms)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Power</h3>
        <pre><code>P = IV
P = I²R
P = V²/R

P = power (watts)
Energy = Pt (joules)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Series & Parallel</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Series Circuits</h3>
        <pre><code>R_total = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ + ...
I_total = I₁ = I₂ = I₃
V_total = V₁ + V₂ + V₃</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Parallel Circuits</h3>
        <pre><code>1/R_total = 1/R₁ + 1/R₂ + 1/R₃
V_total = V₁ = V₂ = V₃
I_total = I₁ + I₂ + I₃</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Capacitance</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Capacitor Formulas</h3>
        <pre><code>C = Q/V (capacitance)
Q = CV (charge)
E = ½CV² (energy stored)
τ = RC (time constant)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Magnetic Fields</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Magnetic Force</h3>
        <pre><code>F = BIL sin θ
F = Bqv sin θ
B = μ₀I/(2πr) (wire)
Φ = BA cos θ (flux)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
